      'The Process: A clay core is shaped, covered with wax threads to create the design, then encased in clay. Molten metal is poured in, the wax melts and drains out (hence "lost wax"), and the metal takes the shape of the wax pattern. The outer clay mold is broken to reveal the finished piece.',
